 \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460],\n  \"window\": [18083, 27683],\n  \"confidence\": 0.80,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1885 has exactly one event/partner in the interval (step_04) and that outgoing contact is to node 749 (step_06). There is no direct 1885\u21921460 event (step_05). For a cascade to reach 1460, 749 would need to forward activity, but 749 has no events to 1460, 632, or 765 in the window (steps_10, _11, _12), blocking any time-respecting chain from 1885. Other nodes (e.g. 632\u21921460) are active and could deliver influence to 1460 (step_16) and activity times overlap in coarse bins (steps_14, _15), so the absence of a cascade is not explained by global inactivity \u2014 rather by the missing temporal edges that would connect 1885's sole contact onward. Hence no time-respecting cascade from 1885 to 1460 is supported by the temporal evidence.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 85495, "total_output_tokens": 7788, "total_tokens": 93283, "total_latency_ms": 97136, "llm_calls": 17, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}